Bug Analysis Report — HeyDots (heydot.ai.studio) — 2026-11-10
Data coverage: ✅ live site (browser) — 9 automated passes at 1440×900 / 768×1024 / 390×844 · ➖ PostHog not needed (third-party site, no project telemetry) · ➖ Langfuse not needed (no agent chain) · ➖ GitHub not needed (nothing read or filed) · 📎 user-provided materials — the URL only

Conclusion
High
The site's single conversion path is broken. Every primary CTA ("START A PROJECT", "CONTACT", "BOOK A INTRO CALL", "SCHEDULE A CONSULTATION", "TALK TO AN EXPERT") opens the same contact modal. Filling that modal and pressing SUBMIT REQUEST renders a success state — "Consultation Request Received — Thank you, Audit Tester! Our engineering lead will reach out to audit.tester@example.com shortly." — while the browser issues zero network requests: 98 requests before submit, 98 after, none during. Nothing is written to localStorage or sessionStorage either. The lead is discarded and the visitor is told it was received.

Second, 68% of in-page navigation is dead: 17 of 25 anchor links point at element IDs that do not exist in the document (#solutions, #architecture, #benefits, #contact, #about, #featured-video, #home). Clicking them changes the URL hash and scrolls nowhere. The entire footer navigation column is affected.

Third, the site has no routing and no crawl surface: every unknown path returns HTTP 200 with the same 1,571-byte SPA shell, and /robots.txt, /sitemap.xml and /favicon.ico all return 404. Fourth, performance is well outside budget: LCP 9,104 ms, FCP 3,976 ms, 505 KB of JavaScript, and a 5.3 MB poster image on a <video> element that has no source at all.

No JavaScript errors, no failed requests and no 4xx/5xx responses were observed on the landing page — the defects are behavioural and structural, not crashes. Nine defects are packaged below as filing-ready DEF payloads. Nothing was filed to any tracker.

