Per-issue analysis — WHERE / WHY / WHO
DEF-1 · Contact form reports success but transmits nothing
Critical
Where
Contact modal (BOTTOM DOCK CONTACT / CUSTOM PROJECT), reachable from every CTA on the page. Component renders a <form> with no action and no method.
Why
The submit handler transitions local component state to a "received" view without any transport call. Confirmed by instrumentation: request count is identical before and after submit (98 → 98), no POST/PUT/PATCH is emitted, and neither localStorage nor sessionStorage receives a key. The bundle contains no form endpoint, no /api/ path and no third-party form SDK.
Who
Every prospective client. This is the only lead-capture surface on the site, so the practical impact is 100% loss of inbound enquiries that arrive through the website — while the visitor is told an engineering lead will reply within 24 hours.
Evidence (screenshot): contact_submit.png — the success state rendered after a submit that issued zero network requests. Open screenshot

